From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:22:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] twinapi: AppVisibility, as Windows answers it on a desktop.

Word creates CLSID_AppVisibility on its main thread as it starts, twice,
and found no such class.  The class says whether the Start screen of
Windows 8, "the launcher", or one of its apps shows on a monitor, and
tells those who ask when that changes.  Nothing here ever shows either,
so the launcher is not visible, a monitor has no app on it and no change
is ever reported; that is also what Windows says on a desktop with the
Start menu closed.

As measured in a desktop session on Windows (outside one, Windows
refuses to create the object at all): each instance is a new, agile
object marshaled free-threaded; a NULL or unknown monitor is
E_INVALIDARG with the mode set to MAV_UNKNOWN; Advise holds the
callback until Unadvise lets it go; an unknown cookie, a zero one or a
NULL callback is E_INVALIDARG.  twinapi.dll is where Windows registers
the class, with both threading models; the interfaces go in shobjidl.

The test passes in a Windows desktop session as it does here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 39dbf3cbdc54e0ab25d0bb1c2bff3ff06a6472b3)

